From 19357c6a21d48c27a38a8cc8ddd5a5babf38092e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitriy Andreychenko <dmitriy.andreychenko@flant.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:44:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] egressgateway: allow egress gateway together with
 CiliumEndpointSlice

Upstream fatals when both are enabled (commit 9768f15c9d, cilium#24833): an
endpoint rebuilt from a slice has no UID, so the manager cannot key it. Deckhouse
runs both.

In 1.20 the manager reads CiliumEndpoint objects directly and CES does not stop
those being created, so policies still resolve. Verified on two nodes: the
gateway node programs an egress entry for a client pod hosted elsewhere. This
would not hold with disable-endpoint-crd, which Deckhouse does not set.
---
 pkg/egressgateway/manager.go | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pkg/egressgateway/manager.go b/pkg/egressgateway/manager.go
index 0d8c62745a..ca8dcab7d1 100644
--- a/pkg/egressgateway/manager.go
+++ b/pkg/egressgateway/manager.go
@@ -192,10 +192,6 @@ func NewEgressGatewayManager(p Params) (out struct {
 		return out, fmt.Errorf("egress gateway is not supported in %s identity allocation mode", dcfg.IdentityAllocationMode)
 	}
 
-	if dcfg.EnableCiliumEndpointSlice {
-		return out, errors.New("egress gateway is not supported in combination with the CiliumEndpointSlice feature")
-	}
-
 	// TODO: refactor config checks for both ipv4 and ipv6, and derive whether the environment supports egress gateway policies for either protocol
 	// We need to make sure that ipv4/v6 only environments only create the necessary resources and don't fail if unneeded features are missing.
 	if !dcfg.EnableIPv4Masquerade || !dcfg.EnableBPFMasquerade {
